            <title>[LU-21157] sanity-quota test_91: mkdir failed after MDT restart, seq_client_alloc_seq rc = -5</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21157</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-quota test_91 ("new quota index files in quota_master") fails with "mkdir failed": after the test stops mds1, removes the quota_master index files with debugfs and restarts mds1, the first mkdir on the client returns EIO. The client log shows seq_client_alloc_seq(): cli-cli-lustre-MDT0000-mdc: Cannot allocate new meta-sequence: rc = -5, then seq_client_alloc_fid(): Can't allocate new sequence: rc = -5. Because test_91 exits before its closing stopall/formatall/setupall, the later subtests of the set (test_92, 94, 95a, 95b, 96, 97b, 97c, 97d, 97g, 98, 300) fail in the leftover state (pool_new failed, setup quota failed, trusted_nodemap mismatch, import is not in FULL state), so this ticket covers the whole test set.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen on the branch with the same error and the same seq_client_alloc_seq -5 in the client log:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre-master-next full-part-2, 2026-11-07, test set a8b4b8b4-558d-4ac6-9a43-ae9416147b8d (onyx-156vm220)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Janitor sanity-quota ldiskfs+DNE rocky8.10, 2026-11-07 and 2026-11-08 (j:71392, j:71395, j:71397)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;review-dne-part-4 for &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19895" title="implement large folio support" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19895"&gt;LU-19895&lt;/a&gt; clio change 65094 PS61 (build 135702), session ee04a5ef-8373-463f-b841-a060f5a0dd48, test set 13e24eb2-7483-4054-b7cd-92836c525098. That series only touches the client data path and did not fail this test in its 31 earlier review-dne-part-4 runs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;No existing ticket covers it (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19256" title="sanity-quota test_91: @@@@@@ FAIL: quota () don't update on QSD, 51200" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19256"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19256&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17214" title="sanity-quota: quota (0) don't update on QSD, 10485760" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17214"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17214&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are "quota don't update on QSD", a different error). It looks like a recent regression in MDT0000 sequence allocation after an MDT restart on a DNE ldiskfs configuration; with this error, 5 failures in the last 30 days, 4 of them on 2026-11-07 and 2026-11-08.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-65094-ps61-fe0d272d5fe8 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/65094" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65094&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
